{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"code","value":"type StructuredOutputStream<T> = AsyncIterable<\n  | Exclude<StreamChunk, CustomEvent>\n  | StructuredOutputStartEvent\n  | StructuredOutputCompleteEvent<T>\n  | ApprovalRequestedEvent\n| ToolInputAvailableEvent>;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L1740","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/ai/src/types.ts:1740"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Public type for streams returned by "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat({ outputSchema, stream: true })"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Yields all standard "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"StreamChunk"},{"type":"text","value":" lifecycle events plus the typed\nstructured-output "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"CUSTOM"},{"type":"text","value":" event emitted through this path:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"structured-output.complete"},{"type":"text","value":" — terminal event with typed "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"value.object: T"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"User-actionable waits, such as tool approval and client tool input, are\nrepresented by "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RUN_FINISHED.outcome.type === 'interrupt'"},{"type":"text","value":" in current core\nstreams. Legacy "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"approval-requested"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tool-input-available"},{"type":"text","value":" custom\nevents may still be consumed for replay and backward compatibility, but\nthey are not the current source of truth for waits."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Each variant has a literal "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"name"},{"type":"text","value":", so a single discriminated narrow gives\nyou a typed "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"value"},{"type":"text","value":" with no helper or cast:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"for await (const chunk of stream) {\n  if (chunk.type === 'CUSTOM' && chunk.name === 'structured-output.complete') {\n    chunk.value.object // typed as T\n  }\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Caveat: tools can emit arbitrary user-defined custom events via the\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"emitCustomEvent(name, value)"},{"type":"text","value":" context API. Those flow through this stream\nat runtime but are intentionally absent from this type — including a bare\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"CustomEvent"},{"type":"text","value":" (whose "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"value: any"},{"type":"text","value":" would poison the union) would collapse\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chunk.value"},{"type":"text","value":" back to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"any"},{"type":"text","value":" after the narrow. If you rely on\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"emitCustomEvent"},{"type":"text","value":" plus "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"outputSchema + stream: true"},{"type":"text","value":", branch on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"CUSTOM"},{"type":"text","value":"\noutside the literal-"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"name"},{"type":"text","value":" narrows or cast explicitly."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"type-parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"t","children":[{"type":"text","value":"T"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"T"},{"type":"text","value":" = "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"unknown"}]}],"headings":[{"id":"type-parameters","text":"Type Parameters","level":2},{"id":"t","text":"T","level":3}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\ntype StructuredOutputStream<T> = AsyncIterable<\n  | Exclude<StreamChunk, CustomEvent>\n  | StructuredOutputStartEvent\n  | StructuredOutputCompleteEvent<T>\n  | ApprovalRequestedEvent\n| ToolInputAvailableEvent>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/types.ts:1740](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L1740)\n\nPublic type for streams returned by `chat({ outputSchema, stream: true })`.\n\nYields all standard `StreamChunk` lifecycle events plus the typed\nstructured-output `CUSTOM` event emitted through this path:\n- `structured-output.complete` — terminal event with typed `value.object: T`\n\nUser-actionable waits, such as tool approval and client tool input, are\nrepresented by `RUN_FINISHED.outcome.type === 'interrupt'` in current core\nstreams. Legacy `approval-requested` and `tool-input-available` custom\nevents may still be consumed for replay and backward compatibility, but\nthey are not the current source of truth for waits.\n\nEach variant has a literal `name`, so a single discriminated narrow gives\nyou a typed `value` with no helper or cast:\n\n```ts\nfor await (const chunk of stream) {\n  if (chunk.type === 'CUSTOM' && chunk.name === 'structured-output.complete') {\n    chunk.value.object // typed as T\n  }\n}\n```\n\nCaveat: tools can emit arbitrary user-defined custom events via the\n`emitCustomEvent(name, value)` context API. Those flow through this stream\nat runtime but are intentionally absent from this type — including a bare\n`CustomEvent` (whose `value: any` would poison the union) would collapse\n`chunk.value` back to `any` after the narrow. If you rely on\n`emitCustomEvent` plus `outputSchema + stream: true`, branch on `CUSTOM`\noutside the literal-`name` narrows or cast explicitly.\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### T\n\n`T` = `unknown`\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: StructuredOutputStream\ntitle: StructuredOutputStream\n---\n\n```ts\ntype StructuredOutputStream<T> = AsyncIterable<\n  | Exclude<StreamChunk, CustomEvent>\n  | StructuredOutputStartEvent\n  | StructuredOutputCompleteEvent<T>\n  | ApprovalRequestedEvent\n| ToolInputAvailableEvent>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/types.ts:1740](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L1740)\n\nPublic type for streams returned by `chat({ outputSchema, stream: true })`.\n\nYields all standard `StreamChunk` lifecycle events plus the typed\nstructured-output `CUSTOM` event emitted through this path:\n- `structured-output.complete` — terminal event with typed `value.object: T`\n\nUser-actionable waits, such as tool approval and client tool input, are\nrepresented by `RUN_FINISHED.outcome.type === 'interrupt'` in current core\nstreams. Legacy `approval-requested` and `tool-input-available` custom\nevents may still be consumed for replay and backward compatibility, but\nthey are not the current source of truth for waits.\n\nEach variant has a literal `name`, so a single discriminated narrow gives\nyou a typed `value` with no helper or cast:\n\n```ts\nfor await (const chunk of stream) {\n  if (chunk.type === 'CUSTOM' && chunk.name === 'structured-output.complete') {\n    chunk.value.object // typed as T\n  }\n}\n```\n\nCaveat: tools can emit arbitrary user-defined custom events via the\n`emitCustomEvent(name, value)` context API. Those flow through this stream\nat runtime but are intentionally absent from this type — including a bare\n`CustomEvent` (whose `value: any` would poison the union) would collapse\n`chunk.value` back to `any` after the narrow. If you rely on\n`emitCustomEvent` plus `outputSchema + stream: true`, branch on `CUSTOM`\noutside the literal-`name` narrows or cast explicitly.\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### T\n\n`T` = `unknown`\n"}
